course: dictionary
lesson: 3501
title: Farther and how much farther
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Farther is a word for distance. It means more far, a longer way away. «Japanese macaques live farther north than any other monkey.» The word tells you that these monkeys live a longer way north than other monkeys do.
explain: Farther can also mean more forward or onward, as in «walk farther». Here you are not talking about a far-off place but about going on for a longer way. Look at the words around farther to see which meaning fits.
explain: In maths, farther helps you compare. «Some stars are many times farther away than others.» To find how much farther one thing is than another, subtract the smaller distance from the larger one.
fact: Farther means more far: a longer way away.
fact: Farther can also mean more forward or onward, as in «walk farther».
fact: Farthest means the most far, the longest distance of all.
fact: Stars in a constellation look close together, but some are many times farther away than others.
fact: To find how much farther something is, subtract the shorter distance from the longer one.
exercise: «Japanese macaques live farther north than any other monkey.» What does farther mean here? | Louder and noisier | Closer to the sea | *A longer way away | Warmer in summer
exercise: In PE, Maya threw a bean bag 12 metres and Priya threw it 15 metres. How much farther did Priya throw it? | 27 metres | 12 metres | 1 metre | *3 metres
exercise: In «walk farther», what does farther suggest? | Standing still | Turning round | *Going on for a longer way | Going backwards
test: «The Sun is about 400 times farther away than the Moon.» What does farther mean here? | A faster way round | A shorter way up | A brighter light | *A longer way away
test: The shop is 300 metres away and the park is 120 metres farther. How far away is the park? | *420 metres | 300 metres | 180 metres | 120 metres
exam: Which sentence uses farther to mean onward? | Sam is farther than Ali | The monkeys live farther north | The stars are many times farther away | *Walk farther along the path
